WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.740
Riverside County Supervisor Jeff Hewitt is
a successful pool construction entrepreneur

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.280
turned politician.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:12.720
One of four elected officials governing an
area of California with a population of 2.4 million

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.340
and the most powerful public official in America

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.620
affiliated with the Libertarian Party.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.320
I always think about is it hurting somebody,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.470
is there something I can do to lessen the
imposition of the government

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.449
and have it instead defend our rights like
it's supposed to.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:30.900
At a recent meeting of the board of supervisors

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.129
when a bill to regulate the sales of home
baked goods came up for discussion

00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:36.350
Hewitt dissented.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.829
I remember back in the 50s and early 60s

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:41.829
my mother would make apple pies for Law's
Coffee Shop

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:42.520
up in Oak Glen.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.640
So back then it wasn't a problem

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.500
I think most people around Oak Glen made them
for the restaurants

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.520
and I don't think anybody ever died from that.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.180
My background comes from starting my own business
when I was 19.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.700
Just digging swimming pools.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.499
Eventually I got to building pools, but the
things I learned about that

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:02.909
were to get through the tough times, bring
in my budget

00:01:02.909 --> 00:01:07.060
and in those really great times, you know,
still put some stuff away

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.920
so I could survive to see the next day.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.420
Before he was elected to his county seat in
November 2018

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.820
Hewitt was Mayor of the town of Calimesa

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.100
where he cut ties with the state fire agency
because it was charging too much.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.380
It's common knowledge around electeds,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.640
nobody goes against fire because that's political
suicide.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.480
So I basically was able to convince my colleagues
over there

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.960
that don't worry about getting reelected,
let's do the right thing.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.860
In 2018 Hewitt, whose largest donor was libertarian
tomato magnate Chris Rufer

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:42.340
spent less than half the money campaigning

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:46.060
than did his union backed establishment republican
opponent

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.320
and won anyway.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:52.370
He says that the Riverside County Libertarian
Party has seen a 42% spike in registration

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.570
since his victory.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.080
The nice thing about being a libertarian is
we could reach out

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.140
to the democrats on a lot of things

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.740
especially social issues that we agree on

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:08.800
and we can also reach out to the republicans
ona lot of the fiscal and regulatory issues.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.070
So it put us in a really good place

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.480
and this is what I think a lot of libertarians
don't understand

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.150
we are the great consensus builders and peace
makers

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.620
and we need to go ahead and market that.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:24.620
Hewitt's district is historically republican
but has skewed democrat in recent years

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.280
something he says he was able to capitalize
on to best his opponent.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.740
One of the biggest mistakes that libertarians
make

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:38.300
is to think that democrats are harder to persuade
than the republicans are.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.180
Now on social issues, criminal justice reform,
we're right there with them

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.150
we've already made a connection there.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:49.410
A little bit tougher is to say look you want
to go ahead and make people's lives better

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.620
economically

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.840
let me show you how free market systems have
worked for me.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.420
Don't even need to use the word Capitalism

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.340
but that sell is a little bit easier believe
it or not than people think.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.820
On our board we have two democrats and two
republicans.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.980
I'm a libertarian allows me to not only build
a consensus

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:13.060
but when there's very contentious issues,
I can be that swing vote too.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.740
So being a libertarian is the most important
thing to me and it's who I am.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.660
And to aspiring Libertarian Party politicians
Hewitt's advice is to pick winnable races

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.440
and focus more attention on the basics.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.760
Like public speaking and social skills.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:32.880
Take toastmasters and get to know how to speak
in public and also make friends.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.580
Like me, get appointed to a planning commission,
you make friends there,

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.750
relationships, you start building trust int
he community

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:44.140
and now people don't care if you're libertarian
or whatever you are.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:48.320
You're going to be someone that they're gonna
have an easier time voting for.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.180
But despite h is electoral success,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.980
Hewitt still faces considerable opposition
from his fellow board members on several core issues.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.040
He dissented from an agreement the board reached
with the Service Employees Union

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.040
that he believed would ultimately bankrupt
the county.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.560
Others on the board, including conservative
republicans voted for the agreement.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.420
I sincerely respect the issues being raised
by my colleague supervisor Hewitt.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.480
He's right on the money , we have to start
somewhere

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.960
and I just don't think that it starts with
going after our employees

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:24.760
I think it starts up here at that dais, going
after the bigger picture issues that we face today.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.000
But Hewitt believes that if he sticks with
his principles,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.180
he'll inspire other libertarians to join him
in the fight.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.120
Pick a race that you can win.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.350
A lot of these local races, they're actually
still very powerful

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:38.090
but they don't cost a lot of money.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.160
From two to four years, maybe ten years,

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.500
all of a sudden you're in a very impactful
position,

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.750
you can really make a lot of big changes

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.520
then it won't be so lonely for me.

